  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 passed on casting Spellstutter Sprite at end of opponent's turn despite being severely mana-screwed with only 2 lands and 8 cards in hand. The 2 mana goes completely to waste. The Sprite would provide a 1/1 flying body for attacking/blocking, and is a Rogue that synergizes with Thieves' Guild Enforcer. Holding it to counter a spell is low-value since with only 1 Faerie it can only counter MV ≤1 spells.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, wasting 2 mana at end of opponent's turn",
      "better_line": "Cast Spellstutter Sprite at end of opponent's turn to get a 1/1 flyer on board, providing chip damage, a potential blocker, and Rogue synergy with Thieves' Guild Enforcer, rather than wasting 2 mana while severely mana-screwed",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 96,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 87,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Declined to flash in Spellstutter Sprite as a blocker during combat, taking 6 damage (going to 10) instead of blocking the 4/4 Thrashing Brontodon to save 4 life (going to 14) or the 2/2 Scion Summoner to trade and save 2 life. At only 2 lands with a terrible board position, every point of life matters. The Sprite's counter ability is very narrow (MV ≤1 with no other Faeries) so saving it for that purpose has low expected value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, taking 6 damage from Scion Summoner and Thrashing Brontodon.",
      "better_line": "Flash in Spellstutter Sprite to block Thrashing Brontodon, saving 4 life and only taking 2 damage from Scion Summoner. The 1/1 flying body is worth less than 4 life in this dire board position.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 110,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 96,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 10 life facing 6 damage from Scion Summoner (2/2) and Thrashing Brontodon (4/4 trample), declining to flash in Spellstutter Sprite to block Scion Summoner costs 2 life (going to 4 instead of 6). With the opponent's board growing (Warden of Geometries coming online next turn), every life point matters. The Sprite as a 1/1 isn't going to meaningfully contribute later given the massive board disadvantage and mana screw.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, taking the full 6 damage to go to 4 life.",
      "better_line": "Flash in Spellstutter Sprite to block Scion Summoner, saving 2 life and going to 6 instead of 4. With only 2 Islands and a stacked hand requiring more mana, survival is the priority.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 114,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 98,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "At 10 life with no board presence facing 12+ power of attackers, casting Fleeting Distraction for a cantrip and minor -1/-0 instead of deploying Spellstutter Sprite as a chump blocker is risky. The 1/1 flyer could absorb 2-4 damage next combat, which is critical at 10 life.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Fleeting Distraction to draw a card and give -1/-0",
      "better_line": "Cast Spellstutter Sprite to get a 1/1 flying body on board as a chump blocker, since surviving the next attack is the immediate priority at 10 life with no blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 100,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Activated Thrashing Brontodon's sacrifice ability to destroy their own Setessan Training - the only artifact/enchantment on the battlefield. This destroys their own enchantment AND sacrifices their biggest creature (4/4 with trample) for zero benefit. The opponent has no artifacts or enchantments. The opponent is at 10 life with all lands tapped and only a sick 1/1, so attacking with the full board (3/3 + 2/2 + 4/4 trample + 1/1 + 2/3 = 12+ damage) could have been lethal or near-lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Thrashing Brontodon to sacrifice it and destroy their own Setessan Training.",
      "better_line": "Skip to combat and attack with all or most creatures. With opponent at 10 life, all lands tapped, and only a sick 1/1 blocker, attacking with Drover (3/3), Scion Summoner (2/2), Brontodon (4/4 trample), Eldrazi Scion (1/1), and Warden (2/3) would deal at minimum 11+ damage for lethal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 137,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 118,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Unnatural Aggression to remove Nocturnal Feeder when the player already had lethal on board with 12 power of attackers against an opponent at 4 life with no available blockers (Nocturnal Feeder is summoning sick, all opponent lands tapped). This wastes a card for no benefit.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Unnatural Aggression to fight and exile Nocturnal Feeder before combat.",
      "better_line": "Skip straight to combat and attack with all creatures for 12 damage against 4 life with no blockers available. No need to spend a card removing the only opposing creature that can't even block.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 175,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 145,
    }
  ],
